<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates generally steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates generally steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were generally steady to weaker on Friday, except for six-month maturities which edged up to 11 3/8 percent from 11 5/16 percent, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>Traders said the drop in overnight money in the past four days prompted many banks to lower their swap rates.</p>
<p>&quot;The slight increase in the six-month maturities is just a temporary aberration. It has no meaning,&quot; said one trader in a major Philippine bank.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks in the country were:</p>
<p>			 DEC 20		  DEC 19</p>
<p>    1 W		11  1/8		 11  1/8</p>
<p>    2 W		11  1/8		 11  1/4</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/16		11  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/8		 11  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		11  3/16		11  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/8		 11  5/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  5/8		 11  11/16</p>
<p>    VAL		23-Dec		  20-Dec</p>
